{"title":"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems#Problem_12\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems\">2021 Fall AMC 10B #12</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems#Problem_7\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems\">2021 Fall AMC 12B #7</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Completing_the_Square)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Completing the Square)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Strategy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Strategy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Logic_and_some_Guesswork)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Logic and some Guesswork)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Just_2_min!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Just 2 min!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following conditions is sufficient to guarantee that integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> satisfy the equation\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed4334b3ae76f385d27c6bb80a0dbc73874bdf7d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x(x-y)+y(y-z)+z(z-x) = 1?\\]\" width=\"282\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/8/cb829338f2fd18c5eaf58d46779efef2e31a6dd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} \\: x&gt;y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/6/636739c8201322993086908b20be3eceb4a7854d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"11\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/c/67cc5445681d3f129bd94256f959ad9fd2f2ead1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)} \\: x=y-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/d/4cd247ef3a16b1d64c943724d8b5991c3c5e2f65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=z-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/5/965c74d2f777d2ff55670a3581b2491bdd7342b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)} \\: x=z+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/0/fe033362483e74682b80c748590496ee8b986201.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/8/f7866e8d131a400e22c91245eeb6ecac4cf7aa76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)} \\: x=z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/802dcd94037877c27bd21571946578560ffa3d22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y-1=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/521d1e3bf47935f5e2037e488c58c065c9ee68ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)} \\: x+y+z=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Completing_the_Square.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Completing_the_Square)\">Solution 1 (Completing the Square)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Completing the Square)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It is obvious <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are symmetrical. We are going to solve the problem by Completing the Square.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be1f70bb6b044ef196a92ab52240e958a9f3208b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x ^ 2 + y ^ 2 + z ^ 2 - xy - yz - zx = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"256\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/2/2829de6c91daa70d1036c65fe4e9388581aef7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x ^ 2 + 2y ^ 2 + 2z ^ 2 - 2xy - 2yz - 2zx = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"311\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/8/8483273f934faafe92f6e9b9770e5a8a1cea8134.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-y)^2 + (y-z)^2 + (z-x)^2 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"269\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/0/d20258310be3455daf8318274224a9d1d28fb6a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y, z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"11\" /> are integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/f/69ff44ae5c298b55c12f05a5d95814d3ea913353.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-y)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/7/797975ca85798ade7c9830ae98f572add12ab6bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(y-z)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"21\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/1/2e16f2b13fa4383c97c5fa56b95ceb7b42a1e164.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(z-x)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"19\" /> can only equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/3/53394b86b82c53287b72ba2f5069422387eabe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0, 1, 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />. So one variable must equal another, and the third variable is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> different from those <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> equal variables. So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55bdade53f471aab49f63d1a734979cc0c636640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"29\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Isabelchen\">isabelchen</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Plugging in every choice, we see that choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b305929a95b53f14a0ad53eba1d8560626e1f28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> works. \n</p><p><br />\nWe have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/b/8cb5c9089dc75106e4c94926b52cac2055bcebfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x+1, z=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"17\" />, so \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/8/d6872ccc0bf390a8b408b95fa4c4fe66335d95e1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x(x-y)+y(y-z)+z(z-x)=x(x-(x+1))+(x+1)((x+1)-x)+x(x-x)=x(-1)+(x+1)(1)=1.\\]\" width=\"737\" height=\"18\" />\nOur answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b305929a95b53f14a0ad53eba1d8560626e1f28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>~kingofpineapplz\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Bash)\">Solution 3 (Bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Just plug in all these options one by one, and one sees that all but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> fails to satisfy the equation.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/6/a1629f710a3c822e3c8aa871cbf234245045cb6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/0/fe033362483e74682b80c748590496ee8b986201.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/4/2948238f9606f1178dec5085d65c7521d0f7b76b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LHS=x(x-(x+1))+(x+1)(x+1-x)+x(x-x)=(-x)+(x+1)=1=RHS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"678\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Hence the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/a/3aaffab0f4c5610b12f5f960dbaabe4db56f9fe3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"44\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~Wilhelm Z\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Strategy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Strategy)\">Solution 4 (Strategy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Strategy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Looking at the answer choices and the question, the simplest ones to plug in would be equalities because it would make one term of the equation become zero. We see that answer choices A and D have the simplest equalities in them. However, A has an inequality too, so it would be simpler to plug in D which has another equality. We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/b/b0b4a78db8f086f7169b9a0cc443e0b9ee0224ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=z$\" width=\"43\" height=\"8\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/802dcd94037877c27bd21571946578560ffa3d22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y-1=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" /> means the equation becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/0/dd0a48bc47ad02b20a92b645c90d19f52f5cc933.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(x-(x+1)) + (x+1)(x+1 - x)  = 1 \\implies -x + x + 1 = 1 \\implies 1 =  1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"578\" height=\"20\" />, which is always true, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55bdade53f471aab49f63d1a734979cc0c636640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"29\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~KingRavi\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Logic_and_some_Guesswork.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Logic_and_some_Guesswork)\">Solution 5 (Logic and some Guesswork)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Logic and some Guesswork)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are symmetric, which means that answer choices B and C are the same, so it can't be either of them. Answer choice E doesn't make sense because it is only 1 equation, which probably won't result in only 1 possible answer. This leaves us with choices A and D. Choice A isn't right because if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is really big and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/7/917fa23955391fe5d4ec74cc01d651360340334b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=z=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" />, then the equation becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/c/0ac590ebac956caacf248034bbe4dd06afba2842.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" /> which doesn't work with a large integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Therefore, the only remaining answer choice is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55bdade53f471aab49f63d1a734979cc0c636640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"29\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~bird987\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Just_2_min.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Just_2_min!)\">Video Solution (Just 2 min!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Just 2 min!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/HeHu_ZlXi8E\">https://youtu.be/HeHu_ZlXi8E</a>\n</p><p><i> ~Education, the Study of Everything </i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lJ-RHZXPV_E\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lJ-RHZXPV_E</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gp0xqp5BsfY\">https://youtu.be/gp0xqp5BsfY</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For AMC 10: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/R7TwXgAGYuw?t=236\">https://youtu.be/R7TwXgAGYuw?t=236</a>\n</p><p>For AMC 12: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4qgYrCYG-qw&amp;t=392\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4qgYrCYG-qw&amp;t=392</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B\">2021 Fall AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=20